00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:14,820
And we add in technical analysis and price
action indicators.

178
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:25,900
And then, of course, all of this
information taken together will define or
determine our optimal trade structure.

179
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:38,180
So, guys, that was our little chat about
technical analysis or specifically where
to use technical analysis and how to think
about it.

180
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:44,400
It's very important to understand where
this fits in, especially as a retail
trader.

181
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:53,260
Now, let's get a bit more specific and
let's have a look at some big mistakes
when it comes to technical analysis.

182
00:24:54,100 --> 00:24:58,940
And this is especially important, again,
for retail traders to understand.

183
00:25:00,060 --> 00:25:13,640
Because, really, most of you taking the
PTM video series, this will be the first
time, your first experience of ever seeing
a pro trader systematic process.

184
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:28,280
And how you actually marry up your
fundamentals and your technical tools is
very important because there's kind of a
best practices, best behaviors path that
we need to go down.

185
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:44,520
So, when we just had our little chat about
where technical analysis fits in to an
overall trade idea generation process, we
covered, obviously, getting a trade idea
solely from a chart.

186
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:56,600
But just as bad is then looking at the
fundamentals to then justify why you've
got the position after you've made the
decision from the chart.

187
00:25:57,460 --> 00:26:10,280
So, imagine that situation for a moment
where the first thing you do is you go
straight to a chart, you pull it up, you
determine that because of the chart,
you're going to go long this particular
stock.

188
00:26:10,700 --> 00:26:19,660
And then when it starts moving around, you
then do the fundamental work afterwards
and then look for reasons why you should
be long in the fundamentals.

189
00:26:19,660 --> 00:26:41,660
That is obviously completely unacceptable,
completely intellectually dishonest, and
through confirmation bias, you're likely
to justify any position to yourself by
looking for fundamentals that suit your
own internal narrative that you've created
by just looking at a chart.

190
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:56,340
So, that's you basically turning the
process upside down and engaging in bad
behaviors, and this is not just something
that retail traders are guilty of all the
time.

191
00:26:56,880 --> 00:27:11,360
Many professional traders do this as well,
and when other professional traders spot
them doing it, they lose a lot of
credibility by doing it, and other
professional traders will actually call
them out on it.

192
00:27:11,660 --> 00:27:26,600
So never engage in that behavior, never
pull up a chart, get a trade idea from the
chart going long or short, and then after
you've got the position on, start looking
at the fundamentals to justify your
position.

193
00:27:27,100 --> 00:27:28,880
You just haven't done any work.

194
00:27:29,340 --> 00:27:32,940
This is totally lazy, and you're going to
get found out.

195
00:27:34,220 --> 00:27:43,380
Next up, think of a situation where you
actually go short of a stock that you're
fundamentally bullish on.

196
00:27:43,820 --> 00:27:56,380
So you've done all of your work
fundamentally, and you've now got a
fundamental predisposition where you
believe that the tailwind in the stock is
fundamentally bullish.

197
00:27:56,900 --> 00:28:15,760
But then, because you pull up the chart,
and the technical pattern on the screen
just looks bearish in the short to medium
term, and then you go short that stock,
that is a sackable offense at any
investment bank or hedge fund.

198
00:28:15,760 --> 00:28:23,660
And then think of the flip side, where you
go long a stock that you're actually
fundamentally bearish on.

199
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:30,560
So you've done all your fundamental work,
and you believe that the stock is actually
going to go down fundamentally.

200
00:28:31,100 --> 00:28:39,860
And then you go long because you pulled up
the chart, and the technical pattern in
the short to medium term on the screen
looks bullish.

201
00:28:40,280 --> 00:28:42,380
This, again, is a sackable offense.

202
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:49,780
And in this situation, it actually doesn't
even matter if you make or lose money.

203
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:51,580
Why?

204
00:28:51,580 --> 00:29:03,440
Because you are literally advertising that
you have no conviction in your ideas, and
that your process is chaotic, incongruent,
and lazy.

205
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:10,720
So these are big mistakes that you need to
avoid at all times.

206
00:29:11,440 --> 00:29:13,980
Do not fall in to these bad habits.

207
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:18,820
Just imagine for a moment on the
professional side of the industry.

208
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:21,440
Imagine two things.

209
00:29:21,780 --> 00:29:32,880
Firstly, professional traders at hedge
funds and investment banks only using
technical analysis and price action
indicators to generate trade ideas.

210
00:29:33,080 --> 00:29:34,540
Just imagine that for a moment.

211
00:29:35,020 --> 00:29:44,400
Do you honestly think at a $5 billion
hedge fund, for example, so a hedge fund
that has $5 billion of assets under
management,

212
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:51,460
they have teams of people, teams of
technical analysts telling them when to
buy and sell stocks.

213
00:29:51,460 --> 00:29:55,720
And they are actually the guys generating
the trade ideas.

214
00:29:55,720 --> 00:30:04,360
And then they go and put on $250 million
positions because a line crossed another
line on a chart.

215
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,760
Of course not.

216
00:30:05,940 --> 00:30:07,260
It doesn't even exist.

217
00:30:08,260 --> 00:30:17,420
No one on the professional side of the
industry is generating a trade idea using
a chart and then putting on a position.

218
00:30:17,420 --> 00:30:28,260
And not just that, no one on the
professional side is pulling up a chart,
deciding whether to go long or short of a
stock or an asset,

219
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:36,220
then putting the position on, and then
looking for fundamentals to justify why
they've got the position on afterwards.

220
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:56,740
And then, no one on the professional side
of the industry is doing their fundamental
work to decide on a position, long or
short.

221
00:30:56,740 --> 00:31:07,860
And then, after they've got their
fundamental predisposition, no
professional trader is then allowing
themselves to get swayed by the chart

222
00:31:07,860 --> 00:31:11,920
and then doing the opposite to their
fundamental view.

223
00:31:12,700 --> 00:31:21,840
So those guys, called professional
traders, that are at the top of the
competency hierarchy, at unconscious
competence,

224
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:25,620
none of them are engaging in these
behaviors.

225
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:29,360
So, just make sure that you don't, too.

226
00:31:29,900 --> 00:31:31,240
These are big mistakes.

227
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:40,560
Before you even consider charts or
technical analysis, so your timing phase
of your trade idea,

228
00:31:41,420 --> 00:31:45,800
you will already have a fundamental
predisposition in place.

229
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:50,580
So you'll either be bullish or bearish
fundamentally of a stock.

230
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:56,660
Do not let the chart of past price change
your mind.

231
00:31:56,660 --> 00:32:05,040
When we get to this stage, when we're
analyzing timing using technicals and
price action,

232
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:13,720
they tell us what we probably shouldn't be
doing just as much as what we probably
should be doing.

233
00:32:14,060 --> 00:32:19,380
So, to engage in better behaviors and
avoid all of these classic mistakes,

234
00:32:19,380 --> 00:32:24,260
try to think of it like a traffic light
system.

235
00:32:25,120 --> 00:32:29,560
So, in your mind, whenever you pull up a
chart, when you come to this stage,

236
00:32:29,560 --> 00:32:37,120
think of it as a technical analysis and
price action indicator traffic light
system.

237
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:39,800
So, let's start at the top.

238
00:32:40,260 --> 00:32:45,080
Imagine you're in a situation where you've
done all of your fundamental work

239
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:50,240
and you genuinely think that you have a
fundamental tailwind.

240
00:32:50,820 --> 00:32:53,960
So, you like your idea fundamentally.

241
00:32:54,540 --> 00:32:59,380
You really genuinely believe that
fundamentally you've got the wind in your
sails,

242
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:03,840
whether that's a long idea or a short
idea.

243
00:33:04,260 --> 00:33:07,800
But, when you get to the timing stage,

244
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:10,880
even if you've got the fundamentals in
place

245
00:33:10,880 --> 00:33:16,260
and you've got some identifiable,
meaningful catalysts,

246
00:33:16,260 --> 00:33:17,720
when you pull up the chart

247
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:20,900
and you look at the price action,

248
00:33:21,820 --> 00:33:26,600
you realize that it's probably not good
timing.

249
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:32,780
This is going to be a red in the TA and PA
traffic light system.

250
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:37,280
Your fundamental idea may actually be
good.

251
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:40,260
You might have some catalysts in place

252
00:33:40,260 --> 00:33:44,860
that are potentially meaningful over the
next 20 to 60 days.

253
00:33:45,780 --> 00:33:51,380
But, the technical analysis and price
action indicators that you're looking at

254
00:33:51,380 --> 00:33:54,900
suggests that the timing is off.

255
00:33:55,960 --> 00:34:00,380
So, for example, the short-term trend
might be against you.

256
00:34:01,260 --> 00:34:02,500
In this situation,

257
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:06,320
you're probably better off not doing the
trade.

258
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:09,440
So, do not trade in that situation.

259
00:34:10,080 --> 00:34:11,920
What you're most likely to be doing here

260
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:16,740
is sticking this idea on what we call the
watch list.

261
00:34:17,580 --> 00:34:24,000
And we'll talk about watch lists in a bit
more detail later in this video.

262
00:34:24,380 --> 00:34:28,020
But, essentially, you're going to stick it
on a watch list

263
00:34:28,020 --> 00:34:29,180
and you're going to sit back,

264
00:34:29,660 --> 00:34:30,660
you're going to not trade,

265
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:34,280
and you're just going to wait until the
timing gets a little bit better.

266
00:34:34,960 --> 00:34:36,500
Or even a lot better.

267
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:42,160
Essentially, what you're trying to do in
this situation is just add value to your
execution.

268
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:51,660
So, adding value to a solid, good,
fundamental idea with catalysts on entry
into that position.

269
00:34:52,460 --> 00:34:57,540
Now, next up is the situation on the
traffic light system where we have an
amber.

270
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:01,240
So, you've done all your fundamental work.

271
00:35:02,060 --> 00:35:03,540
You pull up the chart.

272
00:35:04,500 --> 00:35:07,780
And it looks like that the fundamentals
you've identified

273
00:35:07,780 --> 00:35:11,080
and the catalysts, the meaningful
catalysts,

274
00:35:11,080 --> 00:35:16,680
look like they're starting to play out in
the chart and in the price action.

275
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:20,640
So, it looks like the timing might be
okay.

276
00:35:21,460 --> 00:35:26,540
It might not be really obvious that the
fundamentals are now playing out in the
price.

277
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:30,440
But, when you look at the chart and look
at the price action indicators,

278
00:35:31,020 --> 00:35:33,420
it looks like it's starting to wind up.

279
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:38,300
So, for example, the trend is starting to
turn

280
00:35:38,300 --> 00:35:41,340
and it may continue in the future.

281
00:35:42,280 --> 00:35:45,980
Now, in this situation, you need to use
quite a bit of discretion.

282
00:35:46,820 --> 00:35:50,280
So, this is a situation where you would
consider trading.

283
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:53,640
And you've got various options here.

284
00:35:54,040 --> 00:36:00,660
You can take a half position or even you
can take a full position

285
00:36:00,660 --> 00:36:02,640
with good risk management.

286
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:09,580
And even just taking a half position in
this situation is risk management in
itself.

287
00:36:10,460 --> 00:36:15,580
You are preemptively seeking to add value
to the execution

288
00:36:15,580 --> 00:36:23,140
on entry, but at the same time, you're
acknowledging the technicals and the price
action

289
00:36:23,140 --> 00:36:28,460
and taking some sort of position, perhaps
a half position,

290
00:36:28,460 --> 00:36:30,540
so you don't actually miss it.

291
00:36:31,420 --> 00:36:35,520
So, with an amber, you can definitely
consider trading,

292
00:36:36,100 --> 00:36:40,560
having a half position or a portion of
your intended full position

293
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:45,840
or even a full position with good
preemptive risk management in place.

294
00:36:46,500 --> 00:36:51,340
But also, in this situation, if you wanted
to be very, very careful,

295
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:57,120
very conservative, you may decide, again,
not to trade and wait for a little bit

296
00:36:57,120 --> 00:37:02,880
and just stick the idea on the watch list
and try to get more favorable prices.

297
00:37:04,180 --> 00:37:07,240
Now, what about a green light on a trade
idea?

298
00:37:08,120 --> 00:37:09,740
Well, that one's fairly straightforward.

299
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:13,180
So, imagine you've done all of your
fundamental work.

300
00:37:13,700 --> 00:37:15,920
You've got your meaningful catalysts in
place.

301
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:18,040
You pull up the chart.

302
00:37:18,340 --> 00:37:19,760
You do your technical analysis.

303
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:23,680
You do your work on price action
indicators.

304
00:37:23,740 --> 00:37:36,440
So, it looks like your TA and PA agrees in
terms of good timing for your fundamental
idea.

305
00:37:37,660 --> 00:37:44,140
So, the TA and PA suggests that the timing
is definitely in your favor.

306
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:52,020
So, for example, we have a continuation of
trend or an aggressive breakout or
breakdown of the price.

307
00:37:53,020 --> 00:37:55,920
In this situation, you're very likely to
trade.

308
00:37:56,500 --> 00:38:00,320
This is a green light and you're going to
be committing capital to the position

309
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:06,980
and very likely you're going to go very
close or have a full position size on.

310
00:38:08,180 --> 00:38:12,180
And just to clarify, in the previous
example with Amber,

311
00:38:12,720 --> 00:38:17,600
if you put on a half position and then in
the future it became a green light,

312
00:38:17,780 --> 00:38:20,780
that's when you would put on the other
half of the position.

313
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:26,460
But do bear in mind, guys, you know, this
is a preemptive risk management

314
00:38:26,460 --> 00:38:33,360
and there is no hard and fast rulebook in
what to do in every situation.

315
00:38:33,780 --> 00:38:37,820
It's all situational and you have to do
all of your work,

316
00:38:38,040 --> 00:38:42,020
both fundamentally on catalysts and on
timing.

317
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:46,220
And you have to use discretion or very
obviously.

318
00:38:47,420 --> 00:38:51,900
This isn't a one-size-fits-all rulebook
scenario.

319
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:54,420
You're going to have to use discretion.

320
00:38:54,420 --> 00:39:06,700
But there is a logical and sensible
approach here where you just express some
caution at the timing stage

321
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:12,440
when you're doing your technical analysis
and when you're doing your price action
analysis

322
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:17,800
and when you're marrying this work up with
your fundamental work.

323
00:39:18,520 --> 00:39:28,420
The work on the TA and PA is either going
to agree, disagree, or somewhat agree with
your fundamental work.

324
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:40,020
You have to come to that determination and
you have to take the right action or
engage in a logical and sensible behavior

325
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:44,300
to express that reality when you're
committing capital.

326
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:49,800
So whenever we're pulling up charts in the
PTM video series from now on,

327
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:54,600
and even if you go back earlier in the
video series to re-watch videos,

328
00:39:55,240 --> 00:40:04,460
try to get into the habit when you pull up
charts of always thinking of the TA and PA
traffic light system

329
00:40:04,460 --> 00:40:09,200
and how the timing is married up to the
fundamentals

330
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:19,740
and whether your technical analysis and
price action work disagrees, agrees, or
somewhat agrees with your fundamental
analysis.

331
00:40:19,740 --> 00:40:27,820
If you get into that habit over many
trades, over a long period of time, with
some experience,

332
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:35,680
you'll become way better, much better at
committing the right levels of capital at
the right time.

333
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:43,120
Now, we're going to get into the details
now of technical analysis.

334
00:40:44,180 --> 00:40:47,800
We're going to start looking at chart
patterns in this video.

335
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:51,520
And in the next video, we will be looking
at price action indicators.

336
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:55,620
But here first, we're going to be looking
at chart patterns.

337
00:40:56,240 --> 00:41:03,380
We'll be looking at the most common ones
and how you actually use them in your
trading process.

338
00:41:04,380 --> 00:41:09,320
Okay, so the first thing we're going to
discuss, and we're going to get this out
of the way quite quickly,

339
00:41:10,100 --> 00:41:17,920
we're going to talk about candlesticks and
some basic candlestick formations for
open, high, and low-close data.

340
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:21,640
And very typically, we'll be looking at
daily data.

341
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:33,220
And what you're looking at here on the
left and the right are two representations
of daily, open, high, and low-close data.

342
00:41:33,220 --> 00:41:40,520
So, starting on the left-hand side, we
have a candle with a black body.

343
00:41:41,180 --> 00:41:46,540
And that is formed when the opening price
is higher than the closing price.

344
00:41:47,020 --> 00:41:49,680
And this is considered to be a bearish
signal.

345
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:55,380
And we also have depicted on there,
obviously, the high price and the low
price.

346
00:41:56,160 --> 00:41:58,140
And we have two parts to the candle.

347
00:41:58,780 --> 00:42:01,520
We have the body and the wick.

348
00:42:02,300 --> 00:42:06,100
The body is formed by the open price and
the closing price.

349
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:09,820
And the wick is formed by the high price
and the low price.

350
00:42:10,580 --> 00:42:14,600
On the right-hand side, we have a
white-bodied candle.

351
00:42:15,820 --> 00:42:21,220
And this is formed when the closing price
is higher than the opening price.

352
00:42:21,820 --> 00:42:24,500
And this is considered a bullish signal.

353
00:42:25,280 --> 00:42:31,100
Again, the candle is formed by two parts,
the body and the wick.

354
00:42:31,220 --> 00:42:36,160
The body is formed by the open and closed
price and the wick by the high and low
price.

355
00:42:37,420 --> 00:42:44,800
And really, when we're looking at daily
data and we're looking at periods of 20 to
60 days, which is our time horizon,

356
00:42:45,560 --> 00:42:51,820
you genuinely really do not need to go
very deep into understanding candlesticks.

357
00:42:52,660 --> 00:42:58,360
If you think about charts, when we're
thinking about our time horizon of 20 to
60 days,

358
00:42:59,020 --> 00:43:04,920
and we're looking at daily data, we're not
just going to look at periods of 20 to 60
days.

359
00:43:05,120 --> 00:43:11,540
We're going to look at 20 to 60-day time
horizons in the context of a much bigger
chart.

360
00:43:12,740 --> 00:43:16,160
So, yes, you can go into a lot of detail.

361
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:20,580
And in most areas of technical analysis,
this is true.

362
00:43:21,180 --> 00:43:25,420
You can go into a hell of a lot of detail
about candlesticks.

363
00:43:26,360 --> 00:43:35,540
So, for example, you can look at doji
formations or candlesticks, dragonfly
dojis, long-legged dojis,

364
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:42,260
gravestone dojis, hammers, hanging man,
inverted hammers, shooting stars.

365
00:43:42,740 --> 00:43:49,880
Long, upper shadows, long, lower shadows,
shaven heads, shaven bottoms.

366
00:43:50,520 --> 00:43:52,240
The list is endless, guys.

367
00:43:52,820 --> 00:43:54,220
The point is quite simple.

368
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:58,640
In a bigger picture chart, because we are
medium-term traders,

369
00:43:59,500 --> 00:44:04,480
we do not need to go into significant
amounts of detail.

370
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:11,900
And certainly, we do not really need to go
into any detail beyond understanding the
basics for candlesticks.

371
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:20,000
Now, this is the standard definition and
description of how candlesticks are
formed.

372
00:44:20,500 --> 00:44:26,440
But it also always depends on how your
charting software is set up.

373
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:34,200
So, for example, the charting software
that we're using here, we've got the
reverse situation.

374
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:40,000
So, the body of a bearish candle is
actually filled in.

375
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:49,880
So, the body of a bearish candle where the
close is lower than the open on my
software is actually filled in.

376
00:44:49,980 --> 00:44:51,200
So, it's opaque.

377
00:44:52,140 --> 00:44:57,560
And for a bullish candle where the close
is higher than the open,

378
00:44:58,560 --> 00:45:02,180
in my software, it's set up to be
transparent.

379
00:45:03,460 --> 00:45:07,880
So, just bear this in mind as we go
through a lot of our examples here.

380
00:45:08,960 --> 00:45:14,980
Bullish candles are transparent body, and
bearish candles are the filled in body or
opaque.

381
00:45:16,100 --> 00:45:21,580
Make sure when you're looking at your own
charting software that you look at this
properly,

382
00:45:22,200 --> 00:45:25,600
look into it properly, and get the detail
correct.

383
00:45:26,980 --> 00:45:34,840
Now, moving forward, what we're going to
cover here is a whole bunch of technical
analysis patterns.

384
00:45:35,500 --> 00:45:41,940
So, these taken together form our TA, our
technical analysis checklist.

385
00:45:43,520 --> 00:45:49,420
So, when you're going through your timing
appraisal, you can refer to this checklist

386
00:45:49,420 --> 00:45:56,700
and appraise the chart that you're looking
at by referring to the checklist

387
00:45:56,700 --> 00:46:04,980
and seeing if any of the TA patterns that
are covered here are expressed in the
chart that you're looking at

388
00:46:04,980 --> 00:46:13,060
and understand what the most likely action
is going to be in terms of your timing for
your positioning.

389
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:18,020
Now, of course, this list is not
exhaustive.

390
00:46:18,640 --> 00:46:22,080
You can add to this list if you really
want to.

391
00:46:23,080 --> 00:46:28,700
However, it really is key to understand
that technical analysis and charting

392
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:31,420
is literally an endless rabbit hole.

393
00:46:31,980 --> 00:46:35,180
In terms of technical analysis and price
action,

394
00:46:35,820 --> 00:46:39,780
really, all you have to do at the timing
appraisal stage

395
00:46:39,780 --> 00:46:43,860
is to get the big things, get the most
important things right.

396
00:46:44,780 --> 00:46:48,900
There's very obviously a law of
diminishing marginal utility

397
00:46:48,900 --> 00:46:53,360
to going too deep into technical analysis
and price action

398
00:46:53,360 --> 00:46:59,000
in terms of what value it's going to add
to your bottom line in your trading
account.

399
00:46:59,680 --> 00:47:04,040
Over the 20- to 60-day time horizon,
utilising daily data,

400
00:47:04,840 --> 00:47:10,380
you just have to get the most important
things, the big picture, right in terms of
your timing.

401
00:47:11,380 --> 00:47:14,900
So, let's start with trending stocks.

402
00:47:15,260 --> 00:47:17,600
This is all very, very straightforward
stuff.

403
00:47:18,980 --> 00:47:23,560
So, we're looking here at an upward
trending stock.

404
00:47:24,240 --> 00:47:27,740
We're looking at ODFL, Old Dominion
Freight Line.

405
00:47:28,400 --> 00:47:30,060
How do you interpret this?

406
00:47:30,380 --> 00:47:31,660
Well, very simple.

407
00:47:32,420 --> 00:47:35,700
The stock is trending upwards and it's
bullish.

408
00:47:36,980 --> 00:47:39,520
Now, when we look through all of these
patterns,

409
00:47:39,980 --> 00:47:42,340
we're going to be looking at all of these
patterns

410
00:47:42,340 --> 00:47:46,240
through both a long lens and a short lens.

411
00:47:46,940 --> 00:47:52,120
So, imagine if you have your fundamental
predisposition of, for example, bullish.

412
00:47:52,920 --> 00:47:55,180
You have your catalysts in place.

413
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:58,120
You think over the next 20-60 days,

414
00:47:58,720 --> 00:48:01,320
this stock is going to continue trending
up

415
00:48:01,320 --> 00:48:04,600
or, even better, break to the upside
through the trend

416
00:48:04,600 --> 00:48:10,840
and have an even more bullish move in the
price.

417
00:48:11,920 --> 00:48:13,320
So, you would arrive here.

418
00:48:13,780 --> 00:48:16,180
You would look at this in terms of timing

419
00:48:16,180 --> 00:48:22,240
and you would, first of all, establish
that there is an uptrend

420
00:48:22,240 --> 00:48:23,860
and that this is a good thing.

421
00:48:25,220 --> 00:48:29,480
The technical analysis pattern agrees with
your fundamental analysis.

422
00:48:30,900 --> 00:48:35,600
However, how you execute now is down to
discretion.

423
00:48:36,500 --> 00:48:41,320
So, it can be situational to what is
happening in the stock at the time,

424
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:44,520
your fundamental analysis that you've done

425
00:48:44,520 --> 00:48:48,120
and also the catalysts that are on the
horizon.

426
00:48:49,460 --> 00:48:51,880
So, again, there's no rule book here,
guys.

427
00:48:52,400 --> 00:48:54,280
There's not a book that you can read

428
00:48:54,280 --> 00:48:57,260
that gives you the rules of exactly how
you execute

429
00:48:57,260 --> 00:48:59,820
according to technical analysis timing.

430
00:49:00,480 --> 00:49:04,220
So, imagine you were looking at this stock

431
00:49:04,220 --> 00:49:09,360
and you are thinking of buying $10,000
worth of stock.

432
00:49:09,860 --> 00:49:12,860
Well, you can see it's traveling or
trading

433
00:49:12,860 --> 00:49:15,300
towards the top of this range.

434
00:49:16,440 --> 00:49:18,400
And you have various choices here.

435
00:49:18,540 --> 00:49:20,460
You can either be high conviction

436
00:49:20,460 --> 00:49:22,700
and put the whole position on

437
00:49:22,700 --> 00:49:26,440
thinking it's going to break to the upside

438
00:49:26,440 --> 00:49:27,500
even more aggressively.

439
00:49:27,500 --> 00:49:31,480
You can be slightly more conservative.

440
00:49:32,180 --> 00:49:35,240
You can, for example, buy half a position
size.

441
00:49:36,520 --> 00:49:40,520
Or you can be brave and you can sit back
and wait for a few days

442
00:49:40,520 --> 00:49:43,440
and try to get this stock at a lower price

443
00:49:43,440 --> 00:49:46,800
towards the lower end of the upward trend.

444
00:49:48,060 --> 00:49:49,800
The point here is simple, guys.

445
00:49:49,800 --> 00:49:54,240
Think about it in the context of the
traffic light system.

446
00:49:54,800 --> 00:49:56,340
You arrive here from your timing.

447
00:49:56,940 --> 00:49:58,620
From your timing appraisal,

448
00:49:59,520 --> 00:50:00,920
you're pulling up the chart

449
00:50:00,920 --> 00:50:03,860
and you're trying to determine whether
this is a green light

450
00:50:03,860 --> 00:50:06,560
given your fundamental predisposition.

451
00:50:07,800 --> 00:50:10,360
And this is a green light for sure.

452
00:50:11,560 --> 00:50:13,740
An upward trending stock married up

453
00:50:13,740 --> 00:50:17,060
with a fundamental predisposition of
bullish

454
00:50:17,060 --> 00:50:19,220
is a green light.

455
00:50:20,820 --> 00:50:24,000
How you then execute is situational

456
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:25,880
and down to your discretion.

457
00:50:26,940 --> 00:50:30,680
Now let's think about this from a short
perspective.

458
00:50:31,160 --> 00:50:33,020
As much as this is a green light

459
00:50:33,020 --> 00:50:36,360
for a fundamental predisposition of
bullish

460
00:50:36,360 --> 00:50:38,460
from a short perspective,

461
00:50:38,460 --> 00:50:41,060
looking at this through the lens

462
00:50:41,060 --> 00:50:45,560
of a fundamentally bearish predisposition,

463
00:50:46,160 --> 00:50:48,740
this would actually be a red light.

464
00:50:49,820 --> 00:50:52,120
What you would much rather see here

465
00:50:52,120 --> 00:50:55,080
for you to get a short position on

466
00:50:55,080 --> 00:50:58,220
is that the stock is trading

467
00:50:58,220 --> 00:51:02,180
through the bottom end of the range of the
trend.

468
00:51:02,660 --> 00:51:02,860
Why?

469
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:05,460
Because it means it's broken the trend.

470
00:51:06,360 --> 00:51:08,720
The stock price in that situation

471
00:51:08,720 --> 00:51:11,220
has broken the upward trend

472
00:51:11,220 --> 00:51:13,200
and it's broken it to the downside.

473
00:51:14,520 --> 00:51:16,360
So in all likelihood,

474
00:51:16,880 --> 00:51:18,320
you would be much better off

475
00:51:18,320 --> 00:51:21,660
just sitting back and waiting for the
price

476
00:51:21,660 --> 00:51:25,080
to confirm that it wants to break the
trend

477
00:51:25,080 --> 00:51:26,060
to the downside.

478
00:51:26,060 --> 00:51:28,180
In that situation,

479
00:51:28,180 --> 00:51:32,580
you'd have your fundamental predisposition
of bearish

480
00:51:32,580 --> 00:51:36,480
and the technicals are confirming

481
00:51:36,480 --> 00:51:38,680
your fundamental predisposition.

482
00:51:39,900 --> 00:51:43,620
Now again, there is no hard and fast
rulebook here, guys.

483
00:51:44,360 --> 00:51:47,560
We're not saying here that in all
situations,

484
00:51:48,100 --> 00:51:50,160
there's actions that you need to take.

485
00:51:51,160 --> 00:51:53,200
You could be a little bit brave here.

486
00:51:53,600 --> 00:51:58,540
So let's say you have a fundamental
predisposition of bearish

487
00:51:58,540 --> 00:52:01,500
and you're at the top,

488
00:52:01,600 --> 00:52:04,720
the price is at the top of the upward
range.

489
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:10,980
It would be a bit careless to go and put
on a full position size.

490
00:52:11,400 --> 00:52:14,100
So let's say your full position size is
$10,000.

491
00:52:15,200 --> 00:52:17,540
It would probably be the wrong thing to do

492
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:20,680
and quite irresponsible to do that.

493
00:52:20,960 --> 00:52:28,120
But you could potentially go and put a
small amount of the short on.

494
00:52:28,680 --> 00:52:32,120
So let's say $2,500 or $3,000 of the short

495
00:52:32,120 --> 00:52:34,200
and then just sit back and wait.

496
00:52:35,200 --> 00:52:38,280
Again, there's no absolute hard and fast
rulebook.

497
00:52:38,800 --> 00:52:42,340
You could put, say, the $2,500 or $3,000
short on

498
00:52:42,340 --> 00:52:44,620
and then when it breaks to the downside,

499
00:52:45,040 --> 00:52:46,860
get up to your full position size.

500
00:52:48,300 --> 00:52:53,500
And in that case, you would actually have
a higher average price

501
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:55,280
than the first scenario

502
00:52:55,280 --> 00:52:58,000
than if you shorted it on the break to the
downside.

503
00:52:58,960 --> 00:53:02,360
But at the same time, you are taking a bit
of risk here,

504
00:53:03,000 --> 00:53:06,180
even though it's a small negligible
position,

505
00:53:06,740 --> 00:53:09,040
that the stock just continues on the
uptrend

506
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:10,180
and you're just wrong.

507
00:53:11,180 --> 00:53:16,480
So again, it's down to discretion and
probabilistic scenarios.

508
00:53:17,660 --> 00:53:20,060
But generally speaking, in the bigger
picture,

509
00:53:20,840 --> 00:53:22,720
a trending stock upwards

510
00:53:22,720 --> 00:53:26,200
for a fundamental predisposition of
bullish

511
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:28,160
is going to be a green light

512
00:53:28,160 --> 00:53:32,240
and for a fundamental predisposition of
bearish,

513
00:53:32,560 --> 00:53:35,580
in the bigger picture, it's going to be a
warning sign.

514
00:53:35,700 --> 00:53:37,140
It's going to be a red light.

515
00:53:38,660 --> 00:53:40,680
So all pretty basic stuff, guys,

516
00:53:40,740 --> 00:53:42,400
when we look at trending stocks.

517
00:53:43,300 --> 00:53:46,780
And if we look at a downward trending
stock,

518
00:53:47,320 --> 00:53:51,500
you would obviously expect the opposite
disciplines to hold true.

519
00:53:52,500 --> 00:53:55,200
So this is quite an entertaining chart
here.

520
00:53:55,200 --> 00:54:00,340
This is Tesla scrolled back to 2019.

521
00:54:01,720 --> 00:54:04,400
So you can see here on the chart

522
00:54:04,400 --> 00:54:07,100
that Tesla at the end of 2018

523
00:54:07,100 --> 00:54:11,220
was around $70, $75

524
00:54:11,220 --> 00:54:16,380
and it went down to $35 to $40 around that
range.

525
00:54:17,540 --> 00:54:22,580
It then broke the downward trend to the
upside.

526
00:54:23,620 --> 00:54:26,380
And at the time of recording, 2021,

527
00:54:27,340 --> 00:54:31,460
this stock, Tesla, was $580.

528
00:54:32,640 --> 00:54:34,940
So this is a good example

529
00:54:34,940 --> 00:54:39,740
whereby if you came into this situation

530
00:54:39,740 --> 00:54:41,220
where you pulled up the chart

531
00:54:41,220 --> 00:54:46,320
and it just broken the downward trend to
the upside

532
00:54:46,320 --> 00:54:49,360
and you were fundamentally bearish,

533
00:54:50,040 --> 00:54:52,420
this would have been a big warning sign.

534
00:54:52,580 --> 00:54:55,260
This would have been a big flashing red
light.

535
00:54:56,340 --> 00:54:57,620
And if you were bullish,

536
00:54:57,880 --> 00:55:01,360
it would have been a big flashing green
light.

537
00:55:02,600 --> 00:55:03,880
But if we go back

538
00:55:03,880 --> 00:55:07,580
and we think about the downward sloping
trending channel,

539
00:55:08,960 --> 00:55:10,560
if you'd have, let's say,

540
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:13,880
come into this in March 2019

541
00:55:13,880 --> 00:55:18,480
and you had a fundamental predisposition

542
00:55:18,480 --> 00:55:20,160
that's bullish,

543
00:55:20,420 --> 00:55:23,360
that would have been a warning sign at
that time

544
00:55:23,360 --> 00:55:25,500
for the technical timing.

545
00:55:26,300 --> 00:55:28,620
And if you'd have come in bearish,

546
00:55:29,040 --> 00:55:33,160
that would have been actually a green
light at that time.

547
00:55:34,220 --> 00:55:36,980
And again, in terms of executions

548
00:55:36,980 --> 00:55:40,940
and how you would go about executing your
position size,

549
00:55:41,420 --> 00:55:43,720
that would just be down to the situation
again

550
00:55:43,720 --> 00:55:47,060
at the time catalyst you see on the
horizon.

551
00:55:47,600 --> 00:55:49,420
And it really is discretionary.

552
00:55:49,580 --> 00:55:53,420
There's no rule book in terms of exactly
what you have to do

553
00:55:53,420 --> 00:55:55,460
for your executions

554
00:55:55,460 --> 00:55:57,420
when certain things happen

555
00:55:57,420 --> 00:56:00,660
in the technicals of a stock.

556
00:56:01,820 --> 00:56:06,140
Because we're a 20 to 60 day time horizon,

557
00:56:06,140 --> 00:56:09,340
we don't have to be surgically precise

558
00:56:09,340 --> 00:56:10,480
in everything we do.

559
00:56:11,000 --> 00:56:12,600
We just have to stick

560
00:56:12,600 --> 00:56:16,360
to a checklist of technical patterns

561
00:56:16,360 --> 00:56:20,960
and stick to some loosely held best
practices.

562
00:56:22,960 --> 00:56:25,260
But definitely in this situation,

563
00:56:25,800 --> 00:56:27,940
a downward trending stock,

564
00:56:28,800 --> 00:56:31,240
if you come in with a fundamentally

565
00:56:31,240 --> 00:56:34,140
bullish predisposition

566
00:56:34,140 --> 00:56:36,700
and you're coming into it

567
00:56:36,700 --> 00:56:39,120
when there's a very defined downtrend,

568
00:56:39,800 --> 00:56:41,900
it's going to be a red light.

569
00:56:43,140 --> 00:56:44,560
And if you come into it

570
00:56:44,560 --> 00:56:48,260
with a fundamentally bearish
predisposition,

571
00:56:48,680 --> 00:56:49,660
it's very likely

572
00:56:49,660 --> 00:56:51,580
that it's going to be a green light.

573
00:56:53,260 --> 00:56:55,560
If you come into a situation

574
00:56:55,560 --> 00:56:59,860
where you've got a downward trending
stock,

575
00:56:59,860 --> 00:57:03,700
you have a fundamentally bullish
predisposition

576
00:57:03,700 --> 00:57:07,040
and the price has broken to the upside,

577
00:57:07,560 --> 00:57:08,620
the downward trend,

578
00:57:09,160 --> 00:57:10,580
this is a bullish signal

579
00:57:10,580 --> 00:57:12,380
and it's going to be a green light.

580
00:57:13,380 --> 00:57:15,360
If you're fundamentally bearish,

581
00:57:15,980 --> 00:57:18,100
that is going to be a red light.

582
00:57:19,540 --> 00:57:21,640
And yes, the opposite would be true there

583
00:57:21,640 --> 00:57:24,700
if you had an upward trending stock

584
00:57:24,700 --> 00:57:26,100
like in the previous example

585
00:57:26,100 --> 00:57:29,480
and the price broke to the downside.

586
00:57:30,320 --> 00:57:31,660
In both cases,

587
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:33,360
what's most likely to happen

588
00:57:33,360 --> 00:57:35,660
is you're going to sit back,

589
00:57:36,340 --> 00:57:38,900
put the stock on the watch list,

590
00:57:39,020 --> 00:57:41,500
put it down to poor timing,

591
00:57:42,300 --> 00:57:44,800
sit back and wait for better entries

592
00:57:44,800 --> 00:57:47,980
or even no entry at all

593
00:57:47,980 --> 00:57:51,720
because Tesla would be a classic example
of that

594
00:57:51,720 --> 00:57:53,880
where it was very easy

595
00:57:53,880 --> 00:57:57,180
to be fundamentally bearish in that stock.

596
00:57:57,640 --> 00:58:00,860
But so many times people will have pulled
up

597
00:58:00,860 --> 00:58:04,860
people who had a fundamental bearish
predisposition,

598
00:58:04,860 --> 00:58:08,380
they will have pulled up the stock

599
00:58:08,380 --> 00:58:10,860
and they would have seen in the
technicals,

600
00:58:10,860 --> 00:58:15,180
technical patterns and price action

601
00:58:15,180 --> 00:58:17,760
that would not have agreed

602
00:58:17,760 --> 00:58:21,120
with their fundamental bearish
predisposition.

603
00:58:21,120 --> 00:58:24,780
And instead of listening to that

604
00:58:24,780 --> 00:58:28,940
and realizing that the TA doesn't marry up

605
00:58:28,940 --> 00:58:31,680
with their fundamental predisposition,

606
00:58:32,400 --> 00:58:34,440
a lot of traders,

607
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:36,520
long-short portfolio managers

608
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:38,940
got very dogmatic

609
00:58:38,940 --> 00:58:42,140
in their fundamental predisposition,

610
00:58:42,940 --> 00:58:45,220
didn't listen to the message

611
00:58:45,220 --> 00:58:47,400
of aggressive breakouts in the stock

612
00:58:47,400 --> 00:58:49,440
and they went in

613
00:58:49,440 --> 00:58:51,000
and they were fighting the market

614
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:51,840
all the way up.

615
00:58:52,180 --> 00:58:53,300
And you can see

616
00:58:53,300 --> 00:58:55,540
where the price is now

617
00:58:55,540 --> 00:58:56,520
at the top of the screen

618
00:58:56,520 --> 00:58:58,000
at the time of recording,

619
00:58:58,540 --> 00:58:59,540
$580.

620
00:59:01,180 --> 00:59:02,960
So being dogmatic

621
00:59:02,960 --> 00:59:06,080
in your fundamental predisposition

622
00:59:06,080 --> 00:59:09,340
and not listening to the technicals

623
00:59:09,340 --> 00:59:12,220
can be actually very detrimental

624
00:59:12,220 --> 00:59:14,160
to your returns,

625
00:59:14,500 --> 00:59:16,400
especially on shorts, of course.

626
00:59:17,240 --> 00:59:18,440
Look at the Tesla example.

627
00:59:19,460 --> 00:59:21,420
You can get completely wiped out

628
00:59:21,420 --> 00:59:23,620
when you have a move like that

629
00:59:23,620 --> 00:59:26,400
in one or two years

630
00:59:26,400 --> 00:59:27,920
